--- A function compiled code calls is compiled, even where it is handed
--- only the items of an empty list, whose kind no call says: `notes` walks
--- the lists it is given and hands `note` their items, and the program
--- hands it two empty lists. The compiled program had printed the call and
--- not the function (magpie.manifest's `declare` with no notes calls
--- `with_note`), and did not build; a parameter of no known kind is held
--- as text, as the empty list's items are.
fn note[held, name, said]
    return push[held, '`name`=`said`']

fn notes[names, texts]
    held = slice[['x'], 0, 0]
    for i in range[len[names]]
        held = note[held, names[i], texts[i]]
    return held

log[len[notes[[], []]]]
log[notes[[], []]]
